course: dictionary
lesson: 4240
title: Family words and names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A grandpa is an informal, friendly word for your grandfather, the father of your mum or your dad. Context gives you clues. «Later Mum explains: Grandpa needs a small operation and they were planning the trip to visit him.» Visiting him and his operation show that he is a person in your family.
explain: Families use different names for the same person. A child might say Grandpa, Grandad, Granddad, Pop or Gramps, depending on the family and country. If a text says Pop, read the clues: who is it, and how is he related to you?
explain: In stories, the clues often show a grandpa's mood and what he is like. «Grandpa chuckled: "Well, it worked on your daddy."» He is laughing quietly and teasing in a warm, playful way.
explain: Be careful when a story is made up. «Ella's grandpa in Texas swears every year he's seen a jackalope — a made-up rabbit with antlers.» The clue jackalope tells you the animal is made up. The grandpa is still a real grandfather in the story.
fact: Grandpa is an informal, friendly word for your grandfather.
fact: A grandfather is the father of your mum or your dad.
fact: Families and countries use other names too, such as Grandad, Granddad, Pop, Gramps and Grampa.
fact: In maths and family trees, a person has two grandfathers.
fact: In stories, a grandpa is often wise, kind and full of old tales.
exercise: Gramps and Grandad are both family words. What does grandpa mean? | Your uncle | A pet rabbit | *Your grandfather, the father of your mum or dad | A man who sells bread
exercise: «Grandpa chuckled: "Well, it worked on your daddy."» What does chuckled suggest? | He started to cry | He shouted in anger | He was fast asleep | *He laughed quietly in a warm way
exercise: In a maths lesson about family trees, how many grandfathers does a person have? | One | None | *Two | Three
test: «Ella's grandpa in Texas swears every year he's seen a jackalope.» What does the clue jackalope tell you? | *A made-up rabbit with antlers | A real animal you can see in Texas | A horse on a farm
test: In a story, a grandpa is often described as... | A stranger from another planet | Too young to tell tales | Angry and rude | *Wise, kind and full of old tales
exam: Which family name for a grandfather depends on the family and country? | Only the word Grandpa is correct anywhere | A grandfather is never called anything but Grandfather | Grandpa is a name only for dads | *Grandad, Pop or Gramps, depending on the family
